Solar energy refers to the conversion of sunlight into electricity through photovoltaic (PV) cells or concentrated solar power (CSP) systems. Photovoltaic technology captures photons and generates direct current that is inverted for grid use, while CSP employs mirrors or lenses to produce heat that drives turbines.
The upward trajectory stems from falling levelized cost of electricity for PV modules, supportive renewable energy policies across major economies, and growing demand for clean power integration with battery storage. Companies such as First Solar, LONGi Green Energy, JinkoSolar and SunPower continue expanding manufacturing capacity and advancing cell efficiencies, thereby reinforcing the market’s expansion.
